@Test @TC5
    Scenario: Navigate to a facility with an allocated borrower
        When User navigates to a facility with an allocated borrower "Borrower Z"
        And Facility amount is $1000000
        Then The facility view shows "Borrower Z" allocated.
        Then An editable "Limit" field is available for "Borrower Z"
        When User enters valid amount $500000 in the "Limit" field for "Borrower Z"
        Then The value "500000" is accepted into the input field
        And No validation errors appear.
        When User save the facility changes
        Then The changes are saved successfully
        When User navigate away from facility and then back to it
        Then The "Limit" field for "Borrower Z" correctly displays the saved value of "500000"



@Test @TC9
Scenario Outline: Navigate to a deal with defined primary borrower
  When User navigates to a deal with defined primary borrower
  Then Deal Primary Borrower becomes "<DealPrimaryBorrower>" and Deal Additional Borrower becomes "<DealAdditionalBorrower>"
  And The deal overview page correctly shows "<DealPrimaryBorrower>" as the primary borrower for the entire deal
  When User selects "<Facility>" and allocates both borrowers
  Then "<DealPrimaryBorrower>" is the default primary borrower for "<Facility>"
  When User changes the primary borrower for "<Facility>" to "<NewFacilityPrimaryBorrower>"
  Then The new facility primary borrower becomes "<NewFacilityPrimaryBorrower>"
  And On "<Facility>" screen, "<NewFacilityPrimaryBorrower>" is shown as the primary borrower
  When User saves the facility changes
  Then The changes are saved successfully
  When User navigates back to the main deal overview page
  Then The deal overview page shows "<DealPrimaryBorrower>" as the primary borrower for the deal
  And The changes made at the facility level have not propagated to the deal level

Examples:
  | DealPrimaryBorrower | DealAdditionalBorrower | Facility   | NewFacilityPrimaryBorrower |
  | DealPrime           | DealSecond             | Facility J | DealSecond                 |


 


@Test @TC10
Scenario Outline: Navigate to deal with one borrower and two facilities
  When User navigates to deal with one borrower and two facilities
  Then Borrower becomes "<Borrower>" with Facilities "<Facility1>" having amount "<Facility1Amount>" and "<Facility2>" having amount "<Facility2Amount>"
  And The deal page is loaded
  When User selects "<Facility1>" and allocates it as "<Borrower>"
  Then "<Borrower>" is successfully allocated to "<Facility1>"
  When User sets the limit for "<Borrower>" for "<Facility1>" as "<Facility1Limit>"
  Then The limit is set to "<Facility1Limit>" for "<Borrower>" in "<Facility1>"
  And Changes are saved
  When User navigates to "<Facility2>"
  Then The "<Facility2>" details are displayed and "<Borrower>" is not yet allocated
  When User allocates "<Borrower>" to "<Facility2>"
  Then "<Borrower>" is successfully allocated to "<Facility2>"
  And The limit field for "<Borrower>" in "<Facility2>" is empty or zero
  When User sets the limit as "<Facility2Limit>" for "<Borrower>" in "<Facility2>"
  Then The limit is set to "<Facility2Limit>" for "<Borrower>" in "<Facility2>"
  And Changes are saved
  When User navigates back to "<Facility1>"
  Then The view for "<Facility1>" is displayed
  And The limit for "<Borrower>" is shown as "<Facility1Limit>"

Examples:
  | Borrower           | Facility1   | Facility1Amount | Facility1Limit | Facility2   | Facility2Amount | Facility2Limit |
  | Universal Borrower | Facility X  | $500k           | $300000        | Facility Y  | $2M             | $1000000       |



    @Test @TC11
    Scenario: Navigate to facility with several allocated borrowers
       When User navigates to a facility with several allocated borrowers
       Then The facility shows 4 borrower tags
       And The allocated borrower count is "4"
       When User clicks "Select" button or ctrl+click
       Then Two borrowers are selected
       And Both borrowers are highlighted or checked indicating they are selected
       When User selects two borrowers "Delete" or "Remove" button becomes active
       And User clicks "Delete" or "Remove" button
       Then A confirmation prompt may appear
       When User confirms the deletion
       Then The two selected borrowers are removed from the facility
       And Tags for remaining two borrowers are still visible
       And The allocated borrower count is updates from "4" to "2" 


